feof(stream) returns nonzero when that stream’s end-of-file indicator is set. Supply empty input to this separate example: first attempt a read, then inspect its outcome; do not use feof as a prediction before reading:
```c
int ch = getchar();
if (ch == EOF && !ferror(stdin)) {
    printf("%d\n", feof(stdin) != 0);
}
```
